-- emit/app: a module with nothing reachable is not written at all
-- (`docs/design/backend.md` §5, §9).
--
-- Two modules. `Reached` has one value `main` calls, so it is emitted with
-- exactly that value in it — its other `pub` declaration is dropped like
-- any other unreachable one. `Gone` is imported by nobody: the entry module
-- does not name it, nothing in `Reached` names it, and `_expected.absent`
-- asserts that `out/Gone.mjs` was never written.
--
-- The two halves are one mechanism. Imports are use-driven — `need` and
-- `needDerived` collect them as lowering discovers them — so a module with
-- no surviving reference to another emits no `import` of it, and a module
-- nothing imports is a module nothing can miss. There is no separate
-- "is this module used" question and no risk of the two answers
-- disagreeing.
import Node exposing (Program)
import Reached


main : Program
main =
    Node.printLines [ Reached.greeting ]
